            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Guideline writers are dialing back breast screening recommendations because of concerns about false positives and overdiagnoses. For instance, there's the debate about at what age screening should start. Meanwhile, advocates and some clinicians are pulling in the opposite direction-for more coverage, especially for 3D mammography.</AbstractText>
